# Output of run_equivalence_tests.py. Previously committed and read as
# accurate for 6.5 months (dated 2026-01-14, claiming 21/21 passing across 6
# languages) while nothing regenerated it and nothing ran the runner at all
# (#763). A checked-in result nothing regenerates is worse than no file --
# it reads as current when it is not, and no reader can tell the difference
# without re-running the suite themselves. Unlike test-parity-report.json
# (#757's precedent), no test currently reads this file as a gating input,
# so there's no reason to keep a copy in the tree between runs; regenerate
# with `uv run python tests/cross_language/run_equivalence_tests.py` and
# read the output directly instead of trusting a stale commit.
tests/cross_language/equivalence_report.json

# Generated by scripts/test-parity.sh. TEST_PARITY.md is a status dashboard, and
# CLAUDE.md keeps status/progress docs in GitHub only -- it was removed from the
# tree in #623 but the script still regenerates it, so ignore it rather than
# leaving a forbidden file untracked in every working copy. The JSON report stays
# tracked: tests/test_parity_validation.py reads it as its input.
docs/TEST_PARITY.md

# Stray editor/backup files
*.old

# Stray tooling artifacts
=*
*.log
excalidraw.log
